Exit status 1, 47 lines, finished 16:40 +0800. Nothing the lab judges has changed since the
run above, 68 commits back at `88903bf7`: the registry still serves `chaos-code@0.2.110`, `npm
install -g` still lands exactly one platform package (`chaos-code-linux-x64`), and the
launcher still refuses to invent a binary for `win32-x64`, because the two win32 packages the
root `package.json` pins exist upstream only at `0.0.1-security`. The green half is the same
argument it always was -- the trampoline resolves, the right optional dependency is chosen,
`chaos doctor` answers with JSON -- and the red is the finding, so the lab is recorded in
`scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv` with `verdict=red` rather than turned green by deleting the check
that reports it.

What is new is that a dated row now carries that verdict. `check-lab-coverage.py` refuses a
ledger row older than its 30-day budget for a lab nothing runs, so this transcript has to be
refreshed on a schedule whether or not anyone remembers the lab exists, and the lab prints
`repo HEAD` in its own first section, so a reader can tell which tree a verdict describes
without asking anyone.
